From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 06:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: keep cached original HI16

BusyBox can emit relocation order LO16, HI16, LO16 for the same LUI.
The first LO16 patches the LUI and caches the original instruction by
scan. When the explicit HI16 relocation arrives later, do not overwrite
that original with the already-patched instruction.
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
index 0afc38e..c365019 100644
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
@@ -148,7 +148,8 @@ static inline int flat_put_addr_at_rp(u32 __user *rp, u32 addr, u32 relval)
 		put_unaligned(insn, p);
 		return 0;
 	case FLAT_MIPS_R_HI16:
-		flat_mips_remember_hi16(rp, get_unaligned(p));
+		if (!flat_mips_lookup_hi16(rp, &insn))
+			flat_mips_remember_hi16(rp, get_unaligned(p));
 		return 0;
 	case FLAT_MIPS_R_LO16:
 		lo = get_unaligned(p);
-- 
